 ## Overview
-RenderNet is a deep convolutional network designed for the differentiable rendering of voxelized 3D shapes [S1, S2, unofficial]. It solves the problem of synthesizing novel views by mapping a 3D input volume directly to a 2D image, learning visual feature mappings from exemplary images [S1, unofficial]. What sets it apart from its siblings, such as [Voxel Grid Decoders](2219-voxel-grid-decoders.md), is its explicit architectural separation of 3D feature extraction and 2D image decoding, connected by a projection unit that aggregates features along the viewing ray using an MLP [S1, unofficial]. Unlike methods that extract features in object space independent of camera parameters, RenderNet performs view-space resampling at the beginning of the pipeline, making the features inherently dependent on the camera pose [S1, unofficial].
+RenderNet is a deep convolutional network designed for the differentiable rendering of voxelized 3D shapes [S1, S2, unofficial]. It solves the problem of synthesizing novel views by mapping a 3D input volume directly to a 2D image [S1, S2, unofficial]. What sets it apart from its siblings, such as [Voxel Grid Decoders](2219-voxel-grid-decoders.md) and [GRU Volume Fusion](7543-gru-volume-fusion.md), is its explicit architectural separation of 3D feature extraction and 2D image decoding, connected by a projection unit that aggregates features along the viewing ray using an MLP [S1, S2, unofficial]. Unlike methods that extract features in object space independent of camera parameters, RenderNet performs view-space resampling at the beginning of the pipeline, making the features inherently dependent on the camera pose [S1, unofficial].
 
